      <statement><p>Solve the linear system below by substitution.
<me>\left\lbrace
\begin{array}{rcr}
-2x-5y \amp  = \amp  -5 \\
10x+25y \amp  = \amp  25 
\end{array}
\right.</me>
If the answer is a line such as <m>y = x + 1</m>, enter <m>x = x</m> and <m>y = x+1</m>.
If there is no solution, enter <em>DNE</em> for both answers.</p>
<p><m>x =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>y =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>x</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
      <answer>
        <p>
          <m>\frac{-5--2x}{-5}</m>
        </p>
      </answer>
